    "body": "Reverts b781e95a24bd2d201f4afbe4729635114893cdf5 (#41519).\n\n## Problem\n\nResetting `w_scbind_pos` to `get_vtopline()` discards pending scroll distance when the requested position cannot be displayed exactly. The assignment is in the general non-diff scrollbind path, so the regressions are not limited to tall virtual lines:\n\n- A follower window with a closed fold can get stuck at the fold start, even with no virtual lines.\n- Tall `virt_lines` blocks stop oscillating but leave persistent misalignment after scrolling past them. The offsets accumulate across blocks.\n- Wrapped lines with `smoothscroll` show substantially increased follower lag, also without virtual lines.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Minimal reproduction without plugins or virtual lines</summary>\n\nSave as `repro.lua` and run `nvim --clean -u repro.lua`:\n\n```lua\nlocal api = vim.api\nlocal lines = {}\nfor i = 1, 300 do\n  lines[i] = tostring(i)\nend\napi.nvim_buf_set_lines(0, 0, -1, false, lines)\nvim.wo.wrap = false\nlocal follower = api.nvim_get_current_win()\nvim.cmd.vnew()\napi.nvim_buf_set_lines(0, 0, -1, false, lines)\nvim.wo.wrap = false\napi.nvim_win_call(follower, function()\n  vim.wo.foldmethod = 'manual'\n  vim.cmd('21,50fold')\n  vim.cmd('normal! gg')\nend)\nvim.wo[follower].scrollbind = true\nvim.wo.scrollbind = true\n```\n\nPress `<C-e>` repeatedly in the active, unfolded window. After 80 individual presses, it reaches line 81 while the follower remains at the fold starting at line 21. Before #41519, both reach line 81. A single `80<C-e>` command does not reproduce this sequence.\n\n</details>\n\n## Solution\n\nRevert the original commit in full, including its test. No replacement fix or unrelated cleanup is included.\n\nThis restores the previous behavior, including the original oscillation around tall `virt_lines`. A replacement fix should be reviewed separately.\n\n## Verification\n\nCompared builds of the same Neovim revision with and without the six-line C change, using identical build settings and dependencies. A plugin-free RPC/UI screen test for the fold case passes without the change and fails with it. The tall-filler and wrapped-line regressions were also reproduced in these builds.\n\n## Backport\n\nPlease also revert the `release-0.12` backport, #41795 (`9b7e528426ab7b34836271525cd0de7f4fde3e0f`). `v0.12.5` does not contain this change; the backport should be reverted before the next stable release.\n",
